I will restate the essence of my proposals:

1. In an ontology without categories that are distinct from individuals, lo=
'e/le'e
give you a way to refer to individuals that don't exist in the ontology exp=
ressed
by the other gadri.

2. In trying to grock the categoryless ontology, it's quite easy to see how=
 things=20
we normally think of as individuals can be conceptualized as categories, an=
d
then to reverse that perception, but its harder to see how things we normal=
ly
think of as categories can be conceptualized as individuals.

3. Nevertheless, that ontology has many adherents, and it's not hard to gra=
sp
the essence of, even if it is hard to reason about. Furthermore, it is usef=
ul in
linguistic expression and, in other languages, used.

